# Dev Notes 35 — Runtime Capability Registry Contract v1

**Date:** 2026-06-15  
**Branch:** `runtime-capability-registry-contract-v1`  
**Repo:** `Main-Michael-Sparks/runtime-dev-repo`  
**Status:** Staged candidate; syntax-checked, helper-checked, and contract-smoke-tested locally against the uploaded main mirror. GitHub `main` was spot-checked before staging, but this branch is not repo-verified after push.

## Purpose

Add the next contract-only Runtime Dev substrate seam for future Capability Bus work: capability definition and registry metadata.

This branch answers, in code and tests:

```text
what a capability definition looks like
how capability definitions are versioned and status-labeled
which action/result/event contract refs are attached to a capability
which streaming/cancellation/timeout/approval metadata belongs to a definition
which policy fields are recognized as metadata
which backend compatibility fields are metadata only
how a registry validates definitions and duplicate capability names
how lookup/list helpers behave without executing anything
```

This remains contract-only. It does not make any capability executable.

