## Modular design shape

The `runtime/bus/` namespace remains a contract namespace:

```text
contractValidation.mjs             shared validation result/error helpers and safe object checks
capabilityTaxonomy.mjs             frozen v1 capability/status/event/source-kind constants
capabilityDefinition.mjs           capability definition metadata contract
capabilityRegistryContract.mjs     registry validation, creation, lookup, and listing contract helpers
contextRefs.mjs                    context reference validation and normalization
actionEnvelope.mjs                 action request contract validation/normalization
resultEnvelope.mjs                 normalized result/error contract validation/creation
actionEvent.mjs                    action event contract validation/creation
```

`capabilityDefinition.mjs` imports only existing bus-local contract helpers/taxonomy.

`capabilityRegistryContract.mjs` imports only bus-local contract helpers and `capabilityDefinition.mjs`.

No `runtime.mjs`, `workerBridge.mjs`, `runtime/lifecycle/**`, `runtime/request/**`, `runtime/stream/**`, or `llama_worker/**` imports were introduced.

## Contract behavior summary

### Capability definition

`runtime/bus/capabilityDefinition.mjs` defines constants and helpers for one capability metadata record.

Primary normalized shape:

```js
const capabilityDefinition = {
    capability: "text.generate",
    version: "v1",
    status: "contract-only",
    summary: "Generate text through an approved text capability service.",

    contracts: {
        action: "actionEnvelope.v1",
        result: "resultEnvelope.v1",
        event: "actionEvent.v1"
    },

    requirements: {
        streaming: "supported",
        cancellation: "supported",
        timeout: "supported",
        approval: "conditional"
    },

    policy: {
        maxTokens: true,
        approvalRequired: true,
        allowTools: false,
        budget: true
    },

    compatibility: {
        backendKinds: ["nativeWorkerBackend"],
        modelBundleRequired: true,
        contextRefs: true
    }
};
```

Exported constants:

```text
CAPABILITY_DEFINITION_STATUSES
CAPABILITY_REQUIREMENT_SUPPORT_LEVELS
CAPABILITY_APPROVAL_SUPPORT_LEVELS
CAPABILITY_CONTRACT_REFS
```

Exported helpers:

```text
isKnownCapabilityDefinitionStatus()
isKnownCapabilityRequirementSupportLevel()
isKnownCapabilityApprovalSupportLevel()
normalizeCapabilityDefinition()
validateCapabilityDefinition()
assertCapabilityDefinition()
```

### Capability definition status values

```text
contract-only
planned
experimental
implemented
deprecated
```

For this branch, definitions are metadata only. A future `implemented` value should not be used as proof of execution wiring unless a later behavior branch actually adds the executor/router/backend path and tests it.

### Requirement metadata values

For streaming, cancellation, and timeout:

```text
supported
unsupported
required
```

For approval:

```text
supported
unsupported
conditional
```

These values describe contract expectations only. They do not bind streams, cancel requests, set timers, or request approval.

### Policy metadata

The policy object is boolean metadata for recognized policy fields:

```text
maxTokens
approvalRequired
allowTools
budget
```

It says whether a capability recognizes a policy field. It does not enforce budgets or permissions in this branch.

### Compatibility metadata

The compatibility object allows high-level metadata only:

```text
backendKinds
modelBundleRequired
contextRefs
```

`compatibility.backendKinds` may include strings such as `nativeWorkerBackend`, but those strings are labels only. They do not select or invoke a backend.

### Capability registry

`runtime/bus/capabilityRegistryContract.mjs` defines the registry schema version and pure validation/lookup helpers.

Registry shape:

```js
const registry = {
    schemaVersion: "capability-registry.v1",
    capabilities: [capabilityDefinition]
};
```

Exported helpers:

```text
CAPABILITY_REGISTRY_SCHEMA_VERSION
normalizeCapabilityRegistry()
validateCapabilityRegistry()
assertCapabilityRegistry()
createCapabilityRegistry()
listCapabilityDefinitions()
getCapabilityDefinition()
hasCapabilityDefinition()
```

V1 registry rule:

```text
one active definition per capability
```

Duplicate capability names reject. Duplicate capability/version pairs also reject. If parallel versioned definitions are needed later, that should be a separate registry-selection branch.

## Forbidden-key guard

Capability definitions and registries reject model/backend/tool execution keys anywhere nested, including:

```text
modelPath
baseModel
mmprojPath
projectorPath
backend
backendAdapter
backendOptions
adapterArgs
rawBackendPayload
toolProcess
command
shell
exec
spawn
stdio
cwd
env
```

This preserves the existing model identity/path guardrail and prevents the registry from becoming an execution payload carrier.

## Explicit non-goals

This branch does not include runtime execution surfaces. In short: no Capability Bus execution, no router, no service implementation, no backend adapters, no graph runtime, and no worker/native changes.

Detailed non-goals:

```text
executeAction()
Capability Bus executor
Capability Router
Capability Service implementation
Backend Adapter contracts or implementations
MCP inbound/outbound adapters
Knowledge DB / memory backend implementation
Cognitive Graph Runtime implementation
graph node contracts
graph scheduler
runtime.mjs public API changes
prompt() routing through bus
workerBridge changes
llama_worker changes
configOverride expansion
model path/model identity changes
scheduler changes
init/reset/shutdown behavior changes
observer/event sink wiring
streaming behavior changes
cleanup unrelated to this contract branch
optimization changes
```

## Architecture boundaries preserved

```text
queue-based concurrency remains unchanged
worker remains the model/native execution boundary
parent runtime still owns request lifecycle
parent-side stream shaping remains unchanged
config remains the tuning surface
prompt/output semantics are unchanged
model identity/path is not made overrideable
worker protocol shape is unchanged
init/reset/shutdown behavior is unchanged
```

